# Fallback route, used when the probe in 05- does not answer.
#
# Slacker keepalives than the cable on purpose. This path measures ~56 ms
# with ±68 ms of jitter over wifi, and it is the route in use when the laptop
# roams or sleeps, so a minute of tolerance beats dropping the session at ten
# seconds. HostKeyAlias keeps every route to archie on one known_hosts entry.

Host archie
    HostName 100.126.231.24
    User fredrir
    HostKeyAlias archie
    ServerAliveInterval 15
    ServerAliveCountMax 4

# The same route by address, for callers that have to name it. `archie` will
# not do: 05-'s probe silently prefers the cable whenever it answers, so a
# route enrolled as tailscale under that name is only tailscale while the
# cable is out. dmux and wezterm's built-in ssh client both need the spelling
# that cannot change its mind. Keepalives stay as slack as the alias above,
# and for the same reason -- this is the roaming route.
#
# HostKeyAlias is not decoration here: without it this address would mint a
# known_hosts entry of its own and undo the unification the alias above
# exists to keep.

Host 100.126.231.24
    HostName 100.126.231.24
    User fredrir
    HostKeyAlias archie
    ServerAliveInterval 15
    ServerAliveCountMax 4
